# Backstop only — the write rule is "never put secrets in memory" (README.md).
# This blocks accidental commits of actual credential files, not memory prose
# that happens to discuss tokens/secrets conceptually (e.g. a topic file named
# "auth-token-simplification.md" is fine; an actual *.pem is not).
.env
.env.*
*.env
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
id_rsa*
id_ed25519*
id_ecdsa*
*_credentials.json
*credentials.json
.aws/
.ssh/
